{{!-- The roll-mode radios — one control, three surfaces.

      The character sheet's masthead, the steading's ledger line and the stat-pick dialog all set the
      same three modes from the same RollModes list. They used to render three different markups; the
      steading's was deliberately its own because a stacked column of radios is most of a header
      row's height. That reason is a LAYOUT one, so it is answered with a class rather than with a
      second template: `variant` picks the arrangement and nothing else, the way the steading's
      ledger picks its density.

        · inline  — the words on one line, the live one in the accent. Both sheets' headers.
        · stacked — a labelled column with circle radios. The dialog, where there is room and the
                    choice is the whole point of the box.

      A <fieldset>, not a bare list: three radios that mean one setting are a group, and a group with
      no accessible name is three unexplained words. The legend carries it on both variants — inline
      hides it visually (clipped, never removed), because the words themselves say what they are.

      Parameters: `modes` (RollModes.options — [{key, labelKey, checked}]), `name` scoping the radio
      group, `variant`, and `changeAction` for a sheet's change router. The dialog passes no
      changeAction: its value is read once on submit rather than written back as you click.

      The improvement sheet's editors draw their choices (a section's rule, when a result fires, what
      the sheet does) as the stacked variant, passing their own `modes` and `legendKey`, and `detail`:
      a partial drawn under the CHECKED option, given `detailContext` — the fields that option asks
      for sit directly under it, so it is plain which choice they belong to. Only under an option
      whose mode says `hasDetail`: one that asks for nothing gets no empty box. --}}
<fieldset class="stonetop-rollmode stonetop-rollmode--{{#if variant}}{{variant}}{{else}}inline{{/if}}">
	<legend class="stonetop-rollmode-legend">{{localize (ifThen legendKey legendKey "stonetop.rollMode.label")}}</legend>
	{{#each modes}}
	{{!-- The inline line draws "Adv" and "Disadv": beside the stats it is short of room, and the
	      full words overran the conditions. The full word still names the radio and shows on hover.
	      Stacked (the stat-pick dialog), there is room, and the full words stay. --}}
	<label class="stonetop-rollmode-option{{#if checked}} is-checked{{/if}}"{{#if (and shortKey (not (eq ../variant "stacked")))}} title="{{localize labelKey}}"{{/if}}>
		<input type="radio" class="stonetop-rollmode-input" name="{{../name}}"
		       {{#if ../changeAction}}data-change-action="{{../changeAction}}"{{/if}}
		       value="{{key}}" {{#if checked}}checked{{/if}}>
		<span class="stonetop-rollmode-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
		{{#if (and shortKey (not (eq ../variant "stacked")))}}
		<span class="stonetop-rollmode-label"><span aria-hidden="true">{{localize shortKey}}</span><span
			class="stonetop-visually-hidden">{{localize labelKey}}</span></span>
		{{else}}
		<span class="stonetop-rollmode-label">{{localize labelKey}}</span>
		{{/if}}
	</label>
	{{#if (and checked hasDetail ../detail)}}
	<div class="stonetop-rollmode-detail">{{> (lookup .. "detail") ../detailContext}}</div>
	{{/if}}
	{{/each}}
	{{!-- D9: Advantage/Disadvantage explains what this control does, so it sits on the control as the
	      last item of its row. The advice button's look, but it opens the move. Param: `rule`, the move. --}}
	{{#if rule}}
	<button type="button" class="stonetop-icon-btn stonetop-rollmode-rule" data-action="openMoveBySlug" data-view-state
	        data-move-slug="{{rule.slug}}" aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.rollMode.rule' name=rule.name}}"
	        title="{{localize 'stonetop.rollMode.rule' name=rule.name}}">
		<i class="fas fa-circle-question" aria-hidden="true"></i>
	</button>
	{{/if}}
</fieldset>
